  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the Directly Observed Treatment Strategy (DOTS) and Moving towards Universal Access - Mali (01-Jan-2016-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mali, Tuberculosis, Catholic Relief Services - United States Conference of Catholic Bishops (CRS Mali)This program has the following goals: The aim of the NSP for TB (2015-2019) is to reduce TB prevalence by 25 percent by 2025 (compared with 2013 levels). The objectives of this program are: By 2019, identify at least 80 percent of suspected MDR-TB cases and treat at least 75 percent of these cases successfully.  By 2019, refer 15 percent of TBAF cases via the community.  By 2019, screen 70 percent of cases of TB, all forms (TBAF) and successfully treat 90 percent of TB cases (increase from 76 percent to 90 percent).  By 2019, screen 90 percent of TB patients for HIV and place at least 90 percent of TB/HIV co-infected patients on ART.  Strengthen program management and coordination of TB control activities</narrative>
  </description>
